381
00:50:09,698 --> 00:50:14,718
ばいばいでグッバイ Day by Day
Bye-bye and goodbye, Day by Day...

382
00:50:18,447 --> 00:50:23,727
アストロノート、話を聞いてほしいな
Astronaut, I want you to listen to my story.

383
00:50:24,947 --> 00:50:29,407
君からしたら平凡なことだろうけど
It might be an ordinary thing from your perspective, but...

384
00:50:30,597 --> 00:50:35,227
メッセージは手書きにしてよ
Make your message handwritten.

385
00:50:36,277 --> 00:50:41,177
言葉は宙に浮いてしまうから形に残る方が綺麗だから
Because words float off into the air, so it's prettier when left in a tangible form.

386
00:50:41,947 --> 00:50:46,947
まだまだゆこう！現在の視界は良好！
Let's keep going; our current visibility is clear!

387
00:50:47,487 --> 00:50:52,187
自由落下の旅を続けよう
Let's continue this journey of freefall.

388
00:50:53,307 --> 00:50:57,787
ひとりぼっちでヘルツを合わせた二人
Two people who matched their frequencies while being all alone.

389
00:50:58,507 --> 00:51:02,657
それって幸せだ
That is what happiness is.

390
00:51:04,217 --> 00:51:08,957
ばいばいでグッバイ Day by Day いつか会う日まで
Bye-bye and goodbye, Day by Day, until the day we meet again.

391
00:51:08,957 --> 00:51:14,377
それまで残るぼくらの魔法
Until then, our magic remains.

392
00:51:15,267 --> 00:51:19,767
会いたいの反対の反対、そこが終点だ
The opposite of the opposite of wanting to see someone—that is the final stop.

393
00:51:20,427 --> 00:51:25,187
いまだにぼくら唄っている
We are still singing.

394
00:51:26,297 --> 00:51:31,037
たいしたこともないのに笑えてしまうことがある
Even when it's nothing major, there are times we end up smiling.

395
00:51:31,687 --> 00:51:36,787
きっと、そんなんでいいのさ
Surely, that kind of thing is fine.

396
00:51:39,147 --> 00:51:42,707
別れは青かった
The parting was youthful.

397
00:51:46,137 --> 00:51:50,617
メッセージは言葉にしてよ
Make your message into words.

398
00:51:51,537 --> 00:51:54,477
君の声を覚えていたいから
Because I want to remember your voice.

399
00:51:55,117 --> 00:51:57,677
形のあるものは有限だから
Because things with form are finite.

400
00:51:58,157 --> 00:52:02,387
どこまでゆこうかなんて、言いながらさ
Saying things like, "How far should we go?"

401
00:52:03,437 --> 00:52:07,957
ぼくら皆わかっていた岐路に立ってしまったこと
We all knew that we had reached a fork in the road.

402
00:52:09,157 --> 00:52:13,637
ひとりぼっちと分かれ道は似ているけど
Being all alone and a fork in the road look similar, but...

403
00:52:14,147 --> 00:52:17,337
また交わるから
We will cross paths again.

404
00:52:19,397 --> 00:52:24,207
ばいばいでグッバイ Day by Day すべて群青だ！
Bye-bye and goodbye, Day by Day, everything is ultramarine!

405
00:52:24,667 --> 00:52:30,327
駆け抜けてから思い知った幼さ
The childishness I only realized after running through it.

406
00:52:31,247 --> 00:52:35,987
バイバイの反対の反対、そこが終点だ
The opposite of the opposite of bye-bye—that is the final stop.

407
00:52:36,437 --> 00:52:41,577
いずれ、ぼくらにも訪れるだろうから
Because it will eventually visit us too.

408
00:52:42,197 --> 00:52:44,397
孤独な旅は続いていく
The lonely journey continues.

409
00:52:44,397 --> 00:52:51,117
周回軌道で出会えたぼくらは逸れるだろう
We, who met in circular orbit, will probably drift apart.

410
00:52:53,157 --> 00:52:58,017
声が変わって、背が高くなって、見えるものしか信じなくなっても
Even if our voices change, we grow taller, and we only believe in what we can see...

411
00:53:00,097 --> 00:53:02,547
夢を語るんだろう
We will still talk about our dreams.

412
00:53:09,177 --> 00:53:11,587
中身のない話も素敵だから
Because even empty chatter is wonderful.

413
00:53:12,477 --> 00:53:21,257
まだまだゆこう。ひとりでゆこう。
Let's keep going, let's go on alone.

414
00:53:23,177 --> 00:53:27,177
ばいばいでグッバイDays
Bye-bye and goodbye, Days...

415
00:53:28,177 --> 00:53:32,687
ばいばいでグッバイ Day by Day これでさよならだ
Bye-bye and goodbye, Day by Day, with this, it's goodbye.

416
00:53:33,497 --> 00:53:38,637
ついに解けるぼくらの魔法
Our magic finally breaks.

417
00:53:39,547 --> 00:53:44,157
会いたいの反対は会いたい、それでいいんだよ
The opposite of wanting to see someone is wanting to see them—that's fine just as it is.

418
00:53:44,977 --> 00:53:50,747
